I made and saw a few tutorials on self-supervised learning in the past, but this video by @jbhuang0604 on this is quite something. It covers ideas from InfoMax, contrastive learning, self-distillation, masked autoencoders, JEPA, and world models, including LeWorldModel, all in only 37 minutes.

@jbhuang0604: "I didn't know what JEPA is, and at this point I am too afraid to ask ..." so I made a video tracing the last 30+ years of self-supervised learning, explaining how these ideas connect and evolved.

The video is available at https://youtu.be/How-AI-Learned-to-Teach-Itself-JEPA.
